{
  "chapter": "capstone/failure-labs",
  "tier": "build",
  "notes": [
    "Define fault, window, invariant and evidence before injecting anything. A lab without all",
    "four produces an anecdote rather than a result.",
    "Inspect effect state, not only return status. A call that returned an error may still",
    "have moved money.",
    "Assert tenant isolation before reranking, before prompt assembly, and at every graph hop.",
    "Separate attempted bypass from admitted bypass. The first is the control working and the",
    "second is the incident.",
    "Every bound needs a terminal business policy, or the run halts into a dead end nobody",
    "owns.",
    "Promote each finding to the lowest test layer that can prevent it, so the lab stops being",
    "the only thing that catches it.",
    "Preserve the failed artifacts before cleanup or re-run, or the next run destroys the only",
    "evidence you had."
  ],
  "policy": {
    "required": [
      "fault",
      "window",
      "invariant"
    ],
    "isolationCheckpoints": [
      "rerank",
      "prompt-assembly",
      "graph-hop"
    ],
    "layers": [
      "unit",
      "integration",
      "lab"
    ]
  },
  "cases": [
